1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
WORKS OFFLINE!

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Because kitchens are notorious
connectivity dead zones,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
I engineered an offline-first strategy.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
By pairing local service worker caches
with Dexie for client-side

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
IndexedDB persistence, the app shell
and personal cookbook render instantly

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
even if the backend is waking up
from a cold start.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Offline modifications are staged
in an outbox queue

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
and replayed when network
availability returns.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
ASK AI!

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
For semantic querying, the API builds
a localized RAG system.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It dynamically pulls accessible recipes,
screening them in batches

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
sized to an LLM token budget,
to generate an answer grounded

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
strictly in family data.

14
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Have AI suggest a change!

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Request a change from AI,
such as “make it gluten-free,”

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
and watch the magic happen.

17
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Add a recipe from a screenshot.

18
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Upload an image of a recipe,

19
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
and a draft will be ready to save
in no time.

20
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Add a recipe via URL.

21
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
I built an LLM pipeline using Gemini

22
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
to parse structured drafts instantly
from unformatted web links or photos.

23
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
It handles dynamic recipe mutations
on the fly,

24
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
maintaining an immutable version history
in MongoDB

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
for seamless rollbacks.
